  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Gibran Rakabuming Raka formally resigned from his position as the Vice President of Indonesia. The announcement followed widespread public discourse and reports of legal challenges concerning the validity of his academic credentials heard by the Constitutional Court and the Supreme Court. While some parties, including claimants regarding his degree, have linked the resignation to these legal developments, Gibran Rakabuming Raka explicitly stated that his departure was a personal decision and not connected to the academic polemic. President Prabowo Subianto and the former Vice President provided differing accounts regarding the motivations behind the resignation. In response to the vacancy, officials have emphasized the need to maintain national unity and follow constitutional procedures to ensure the continuity of government administration and public services during this transition.",
